From 8b7d6b3697705cb630072ae6e05111f2f3427152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:32:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09271/11362] Measure the eval budget on real numbers instead
 of 3090 extrapolations

Every induce budget in this project traces to measurements on two RTX 3090s
behind Thunderbolt 3 eGPUs (PCIe gen 3 x4). The scored eval runs on a 96 GB RTX
6000 Blackwell. Nothing had ever been measured on that substrate, so these
constants were sized for hardware the eval does not use.

Measured: single card, Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M, n_ctx 98304, q8_0 KV ->
19,912 MiB of 24,576 (fits, 4.6 GB spare), decode 41.05 tok/s against
35.5 tok/s layer-split across both cards.

The layer split costs 14%, not the large factor the Thunderbolt link suggests.
With -sm layer only the hidden state crosses per token (~10 KB, ~10 us against
a 28 ms token), so the link is not on the critical path -- serialization is.
Two independent single-card servers give 2.31x local throughput on hardware
already present.

That also validated the external Blackwell figure: against a clean single-card
baseline the benchmark ratio is 1.93x, and the memory-bandwidth ratio predicts
1.92x. Agreement to 1% means decode is bandwidth-bound as expected, so 79.37
tok/s is usable here. First Blackwell estimate in the project with a
consistency check behind it.

Two claims made earlier in the session were wrong and are withdrawn:
  1. "tries=3 is a hidden 3x multiplier." Measured 1.00 attempts per induce;
     every cell accepted on attempt 0. The three identical 16,945-token
     generations suggesting otherwise were truncated at a cap, from the pre-fix
     overrun config.
  2. Per-induce cost computed from 16,945-token generations. Real generations
     are 49,244 to 83,544 tokens (n=7, all stop=eos), median 61,284.

Qwen3.8 submission feasibility on those numbers. VRAM is not the constraint: at
K=4 with the full observed 103,717-cell per-slot context the card needs 37,929
MiB of 98,304. The blocker is a config default -- the shipped pool is
106,496 = 4 x (22,352 + 4,096), giving 26,624 cells per slot against 103,717
required. The 4,096 completion budget has no recorded rationale; the only note
on it argues 2,048 was too small. Wall-clock is the real cost: 49% of the 12h
eval at K=4 on the median generation, 67% on the worst. K=8 halves that and
still fits.

Excludes the evidence directory from ruff, matching the existing exclusion for
the previous head-to-head's engine snapshots. These are raw LLM output kept to
show what the model emitted; auto-fixing them would edit the measurement record.

Also restores three results artifacts that a test run rewrote at 17:28:03.
experiment_1736 had lost its flagged_adversarial stamp and corrigendum block;
2031 and 1822 had re-run timestamps and synth timings. Restored from git rather
than re-derived, per never-prune.
